{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACwLFT4FhtZMzdg29C22F9","type":"tool_result","content":" M jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n?? .claude/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .mcp.json\n?? opencode.json\n---DIFF---\ndiff --git a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\nindex 696ec05..3106bd7 100644\n--- a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n+++ b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n@@ -1 +1,37 @@\n extends Area3D\n+\n+## Speed applied to the player along the pad's surface normal, far exceeding a normal jump.\n+@export var launch_speed := 27.0\n+## How squashed the cap gets at the instant of launch.\n+@export var squash_scale := Vector3(1.35, 0.55, 1.35)\n+## How long the cap takes to spring back to its resting shape.\n+@export var rebound_duration := 0.6\n+\n+@onready var _mushroom: Node3D = %mushroom\n+@onready var _mushroom_rest_scale: Vector3 = _mushroom.scale\n+\n+var _rebound_tween: Tween\n+\n+\n+func _ready() -> void:\n+\tbody_entered.connect(_on_body_entered)\n+\n+\n+func _on_body_entered(body: Node3D) -> void:\n+\tif not body is Player:\n+\t\treturn\n+\n+\tvar launch_direction := global_transform.basis.y.normalized()\n+\tbody.velocity = launch_direction * launch_speed\n+\n+\t_play_bounce_animation()\n+\n+\n+func _play_bounce_animation() -> void:\n+\tif _rebound_tween:\n+\t\t_rebound_tween.kill()\n+\n+\t_mushroom.scale = squash_scale\n+\t_rebound_tween = create_tween()\n+\t_rebound_tween.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_ELASTIC).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\n+\t_rebound_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", _mushroom_rest_scale, rebound_duration)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dc0af6d-cbe0-4c02-b838-3375501a9752","uuid":"de318f5b-3608-4e4c-8dd7-1cd39e807bfb","timestamp":"2026-07-12T22:53:27.756Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" M jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n?? .claude/\n?? .gemini/\n?? .mcp.json\n?? opencode.json\n---DIFF---\ndiff --git a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\nindex 696ec05..3106bd7 100644\n--- a/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n+++ b/jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd\n@@ -1 +1,37 @@\n extends Area3D\n+\n+## Speed applied to the player along the pad's surface normal, far exceeding a normal jump.\n+@export var launch_speed := 27.0\n+## How squashed the cap gets at the instant of launch.\n+@export var squash_scale := Vector3(1.35, 0.55, 1.35)\n+## How long the cap takes to spring back to its resting shape.\n+@export var rebound_duration := 0.6\n+\n+@onready var _mushroom: Node3D = %mushroom\n+@onready var _mushroom_rest_scale: Vector3 = _mushroom.scale\n+\n+var _rebound_tween: Tween\n+\n+\n+func _ready() -> void:\n+\tbody_entered.connect(_on_body_entered)\n+\n+\n+func _on_body_entered(body: Node3D) -> void:\n+\tif not body is Player:\n+\t\treturn\n+\n+\tvar launch_direction := global_transform.basis.y.normalized()\n+\tbody.velocity = launch_direction * launch_speed\n+\n+\t_play_bounce_animation()\n+\n+\n+func _play_bounce_animation() -> void:\n+\tif _rebound_tween:\n+\t\t_rebound_tween.kill()\n+\n+\t_mushroom.scale = squash_scale\n+\t_rebound_tween = create_tween()\n+\t_rebound_tween.set_trans(Tween.TRANS_ELASTIC).set_ease(Tween.EASE_OUT)\n+\t_rebound_tween.tween_property(_mushroom, \"scale\", _mushroom_rest_scale, rebound_duration)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Ccxz6crDhKUtAqFbZHdha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the one file changed, as expected — the untracked `.claude/`, `.gemini/`, `.mcp.json`, `opencode.json` predate this session and are unrelated. The implementation is complete:\n\n**`jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`** now:\n1. Detects contact via the existing `Area3D.body_entered` signal, filtering with `body is Player` (same idiom used by `coin.gd`, `death_plane.gd`, `bee_bot.gd`) — non-player bodies are ignored entirely, satisfying \"pass through without triggering.\"\n2. Sets `body.velocity` directly to `pad_up_direction * launch_speed`, a full overwrite rather than an additive impulse — so incoming momentum never carries through, and the result is identical whether the player walked, sprinted, or fell onto it. Because it's a real velocity change fed into the existing `move_and_slide()` loop, collisions with ceilings/walls mid-air still resolve naturally, and the player's existing air-control code (which runs regardless of floor state) keeps working untouched.\n3. Uses `global_transform.basis.y.normalized()` for launch direction, so a flat pad launches straight up and a tilted pad launches up-and-outward along its surface normal — verified with a 30° tilt test.\n4. `launch_speed = 27.0` sends the player roughly 11–13m high, vs. the player's own max jump height of ~2.8m.\n5. The cap (`%mushroom`) snaps instantly to a squashed scale, then a `Tween` with `TRANS_ELASTIC`/`EASE_OUT` springs it back to rest, naturally overshooting into a wobble before settling — and any in-flight tween is killed and restarted on each new contact.\n\nI validated this with a temporary headless test scene (instantiating the real `Player` and `JumpingPad` scenes, driven through real physics) confirming: momentum reset, correct tilted launch direction/magnitude, re-triggering squash on repeat contact, elastic settle-to-rest, and tha